abel><text>Method and limitations</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-method-and-limitations"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-22" playOrder="22"><navLabel><text>3. The price of the American lead</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-23" playOrder="23"><navLabel><text>Someone else’s model can become your product</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-someone-elses-model-can-become-your-product"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-24" playOrder="24"><navLabel><text>The licence determines who can sell what</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-the-licence-determines-who-can-sell-what"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-25" playOrder="25"><navLabel><text>Two tests, two different performance gaps</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-two-tests-two-different-performance-gaps"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-26" playOrder="26"><navLabel><text>From token prices to the actual bill</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-from-token-prices-to-the-actual-bill"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-27" playOrder="27"><navLabel><text>Simulation: the cost of checking the work</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-simulation-the-cost-of-checking-the-work"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-28" playOrder="28"><navLabel><text>Making the exit option usable</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-making-the-exit-option-usable"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-29" playOrder="29"><navLabel><text>Chinese weights can fill American data centres</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-chinese-weights-can-fill-american-data-centres"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-30" playOrder="30"><navLabel><text>Diverging American business interests</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-diverging-american-business-interests"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-31" playOrder="31"><navLabel><text>Matching the rule to the problem</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-matching-the-rule-to-the-problem"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-32" playOrder="32"><navLabel><text>A technical lead still needs a buyer</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-a-technical-lead-still-needs-a-buyer"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-33" playOrder="33"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-sources"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-34" playOrder="34"><navLabel><text>Method and limitations</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-method-and-limitations"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-35" playOrder="35"><navLabel><text>4. The factory test</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml"/><navPoint id="nav-36" playOrder="36"><navLabel><text>From model weights to machines</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-from-model-weights-to-machines"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-37" playOrder="37"><navLabel><text>Sometimes the processor is waiting</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-sometimes-the-processor-is-waiting"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-38" playOrder="38"><navLabel><text>From printed circuits to usable chips</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-from-printed-circuits-to-usable-chips"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-39" playOrder="39"><navLabel><text>Smaller features, different measurements</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-smaller-features-different-measurements"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-40" playOrder="40"><navLabel><text>From system tests to deliveries</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-from-system-tests-to-deliveries"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-41" playOrder="41"><navLabel><text>Processors, software and switching costs</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-processors-software-and-switching-costs"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-42" playOrder="42"><navLabel><text>Controls also change the customer’s calculation</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-controls-also-change-the-customers-calculation"/></navPoint><n